  m_Name: Tutorial_en-US
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en-US
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 121d2593dc3814971a291e9113bfca9a, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 7397695488
    m_Localized: Tap on boxes and <color=#3abb00>avoid traps</color>. If you open
      all boxes around the trap it becomes deactivated.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 21359206850560
    m_Localized: Boxes that don't have <color=#3abb00>at least one number around</color>
      are not traps and contain something useful...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 692387511787520
    m_Localized: When you have <color=#3abb00>3 same units</color> they merge into
      one with higher grade and upgraded stats.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1417033706102784
    m_Localized: A number in the cell indicates <color=#3abb00>how many traps are
      located around it.</color>
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1915867725029376
    m_Localized: "Stage is clear <color=#3abb00>when all traps are triggered or deactivated</color>.
      \nNow it's time to try yourself. Good luck!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3331781360082944
    m_Localized: On the top panel you can check <color=#3abb00>how many traps, boosters
      and units</color> are left on the field.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 18791379550330880
    m_Localized: Let's talk about <color=#3abb00>boosters</color>. E.g. antifreeze
      saves units from being frozen.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 18792206100848640
    m_Localized: While there is no target, boosters are <color=#3abb00>stored in
      your backpack and automatically used</color> when neccessary.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 29646175618457600
    m_Localized: If you <color=#3abb00>tap on a box which is empty</color> the chain
      reaction opens all other empty boxes around it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
